  "answer_text": "Depending on what you are trying to do, **\"iCloud Control\"** typically refers to one of three things:\n\n---\n\n### 1. The \"iCloud Control\" Mac Utility (Selective Sync)\nIf you are a Mac user, **iCloud Control** is a popular, free third-party open-source utility. \n* **What it does:** It gives you precise control over your iCloud Drive on macOS by allowing **selective synchronization**. While Apple handles this automatically in the background, this tool lets you manually \"evict\" (remove local copies of) files or folders to free up hard drive space, or force-download items to ensure they are available offline.\n* **How to get it:** You can download it directly from GitHub (by developer *Obbut*) or install it via Homebrew using your Mac Terminal:\n  ```bash\n  brew install --cask icloud-control\n  ```\n\n---\n\n### 2. The \"iCloud Control Panel\" (iCloud for Windows)\nIf you are on a Windows PC, \"iCloud Control Panel\" was the original name for Apple's official desktop application. Apple has since rebranded it to **iCloud for Windows**.\n* **What it does:** It bridges your Windows PC with your Apple ecosystem. It lets you access and sync your iCloud Photos, iCloud Drive files, Safari Bookmarks (with Chrome/Firefox/Edge), Passwords/Keychain, and iCloud Mail/Contacts/Calendars (via Outlook) directly on your PC.\n* **How to get it:** You can download the latest version for free directly from the **Microsoft Store** on Windows 10 or 11.\n\n---\n\n### 3. General iCloud Settings (Controlling Your Account & Storage)\nIf you are simply looking to manage, turn off, or control what your device backs up to iCloud, you can access the built-in control menus on your devices:\n\n* **On iPhone or iPad:** \n  1. Open the **Settings** app.\n  2. Tap **your name** at the very top.\n  3. Tap **iCloud** to view your storage, toggle which apps sync to the cloud, or manage your backups.\n* **On a Mac:**\n  1. Open the **Apple Menu (\uf8ff)** in the top-left corner.\n  2. Select **System Settings**.\n  3. Click **your name** at the top left, then select **iCloud** on the right side.\n* **On any device via a browser:**\n  * Go to **[iCloud.com](https://www.icloud.com)**, sign in with your Apple ID, and manage your files, photos, and settings directly from the web.",
